From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:52:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] avfilter/bt2408_hable: add a Hable tone map on IPT intensity

Port the libplacebo v7.360.1 colour map for its default-like Hable
setting: the Hable curve is applied to the PQ-encoded intensity of IPT,
chroma is scaled towards the intensity axis as the curve compresses it,
and the result is clipped into BT.709 and encoded for a BT.1886 display
with a 1000:1 contrast. The tone curve is a 256-entry table built once
per peak, so the per-pixel work is two 3x3 matrices, six PQ conversions
and one table lookup.

The context struct holds only 32-bit members so that GPU filters can
upload it unchanged. A unit test checks seven colours against a
separate double precision model, a planted wrong peak, the clamp of
peaks below 100 cd/m^2 and the refusal of bad peaks and non-D65
primaries.

Signed-off-by: lusoris <lusoris@proton.me>
---
